note for_latch_i8: a signed for counter that the body writes to its maximum. The latch adds 1 and that add
note overflows: omc traps 1 (exit 101). front-ir lowered the latch as an unchecked add, so the counter wrapped
note to -128 and the loop ran on to its bound (trap 4, exit 104). Bug hunt, ledger L1060.
fn main to int
n = ulong 0
for k byte 100 bound 1000
n = add n 1
k = 127
end
ret int n
end
